-- cpl_memory rows for S693 (SkyKittiwake), the plain session of 2026-11-20, at its Rule 9 checkpoint: M-IDs first, the
-- Closest M-ID column, and what the session learned building it.
-- Applied by supabase-migrate.yml (kb/migrations/.apply), never Execute SQL. INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING.
-- Five rulings in Sam's own words (verified by him in session) and six of the session's own rows (proposed): two
-- decisions, one fact, three pitfalls. Every summary is at most 400 characters, checked by a script before commit.
-- Sam's words: CPLBrain/03-professional/braindumps/braindump-2026-11-20-2100-mids-first-closest-mid-and-the-hand-over-note.md
-- ROLLBACK: kb/migrations/2026-11-20_s693_checkpoint_memory_rows_rollback.sql
insert into public.cpl_memory (slug,kind,title,summary,tags,status,source,verified_by,verified_at,author,event_date) values
('r-mids-first-then-course-exhibit-titles-sam-2026-11-20','decision','M-IDs come first, then the titles of course-based exhibits','Sam, 2026-11-20, in session: "as we get commons re-established through this process, my priority will be the mids so i can then finish the exhibit titles for course-based exhibits that rely on cid/ccn/mid (ccrs)". The M-ID work leads the Commons queue; the common exhibit titles for course-based exhibits follow it.',array['commons','m-id','exhibits','priority','sam-ruling'],'verified','Sam, in session 2026-11-20 (S693)','Sam (in session)',now(),'SkyKittiwake (S693)','2026-11-20'),
('r-closest-mid-column-sam-2026-11-20','decision','A Closest M-ID column with a confidence score and a link to curate','Sam, 2026-11-20, in session: "maybe a new column with your recommended closest mid based on any available new data we have (course descriptions, slos, objectives if available) to get a confidence score with the recommended mid with a link to open a sidebar to curate". Built in S693: kb/_closest_mid.py, kb/coci_closest_mid.json, a Courses List column and a panel section.',array['commons','m-id','courses-list','closest-mid','sam-ruling'],'verified','Sam, in session 2026-11-20 (S693)','Sam (in session)',now(),'SkyKittiwake (S693)','2026-11-20'),
('r-needs-an-mid-leaves-out-cid-ccn-sam-2026-11-20','decision','Needs an M-ID leaves out courses with a C-ID or CCN, and titles open the panel','Sam, 2026-11-20, in session: "click no-mid-courses and the course list was filtered correctly but includes courses with cid and ccn, which don''t need a mid...advise...also need links to sidebar to take action on assigning to a mid". Built in S693: the No M-ID and No identity chips are one, Needs an M-ID (2,508); the 36 with a C-ID or CCN left; titles open the panel.',array['commons','m-id','courses-list','sam-ruling'],'verified','Sam, in session 2026-11-20 (S693)','Sam (in session)',now(),'SkyKittiwake (S693)','2026-11-20'),
('r-subjects-card-on-the-commons-sam-2026-11-20','decision','A Subjects card on the Commons for common subjects and local subject titles','Sam, 2026-11-20, in session: "don''t we need a commons card for subjects to house the common subjects and local subject titles we''ll be establishing from catalog data?" Not built yet: the card sits on the Commons front beside the Common Subjects Reference count, with each college''s subject code and printed name from kb/hand_filed_catalogs/courses/ (16 colleges so far).',array['commons','subjects','common-subjects-reference','sam-ruling'],'verified','Sam, in session 2026-11-20 (S693)','Sam (in session)',now(),'SkyKittiwake (S693)','2026-11-20'),
('r-jev-for-binary-decisions-at-scale-sam-2026-11-20','decision','Jev for the fast yes-or-no decisions over large sets','Sam, 2026-11-20, in session, on the Closest M-ID recommender: "might need jev in this process that has to scan large datasets to make binary decisions fast". Read as Jev the recommender''s second stage: a same-course yes or no on the top candidates for each course in the pile. kb/_jev_harvest.py is the repo''s Jev caller. Not built yet.',array['commons','m-id','closest-mid','jev','sam-ruling'],'verified','Sam, in session 2026-11-20 (S693)','Sam (in session)',now(),'SkyKittiwake (S693)','2026-11-20'),
('d-answered-course-leaves-the-to-do-2026-11-20','decision','A course a person answered leaves the to-do and stays listed','S693 (SkyKittiwake), 2026-11-20: a still-taught course whose hand-over a person answered (a pasted description, or a note that it is not in the catalog) carries answered, leaves the to-do count and stays listed as answered; its outcomes are still missing, and the page says so. His to revise. Built in PR 3613 (the 12 hunt courses; kb/hand_filed_catalogs/handed_over/courses.json).',array['commons','hand-over','to-do','decide-and-record'],'proposed','PR 3613 (claude/s693-file-handovers); kb/reference/blocked_catalog_hunt.json',null,null,'SkyKittiwake (S693)','2026-11-20'),
('d-assign-from-panel-waits-on-the-build-2026-11-20','decision','Assign from the panel waits on a build change, a dry run and a second read','S693, 2026-11-20: the save is kb_curation CN:<control number> merge_into, the row SkyView writes. The daily build fills a re-homed course''s fields from the identity file alone (cn_fields), so a course outside it could land with empty fields. Order: the build reads the state list for such a course, a dry run, a second read, then the control. His to revise.',array['commons','m-id','skyview','kb_curation','decide-and-record'],'proposed','kb/_closest_mid.py; docs/reference/lanes/commons.md (Closest M-ID NEXT 3) on claude/s693-closest-mid',null,null,'SkyKittiwake (S693)','2026-11-20'),
('f-closest-mid-measured-2026-11-20','fact','Closest M-ID measured: 0.75 or more is right 93% of the time; most of the pile needs new M-IDs','S693, 2026-11-20: kb/_closest_mid.py ranks common courses by title, subject, units and description (never TOP). On 6,000 courses holding an M-ID, each taken out of its own common course, a score of 0.75 or more was right for 2,266 of 2,438 (93%); below 0.65, under four in ten. Of the 2,508 that need an M-ID, 82 score 0.75 or more and 56 score 0.65 to 0.75: most need new M-IDs.',array['commons','m-id','closest-mid','measured'],'proposed','kb/_closest_mid.py and kb/coci_closest_mid.json on claude/s693-closest-mid (85a36ff4)',null,null,'SkyKittiwake (S693)','2026-11-20'),
('p-test-tied-to-a-live-worklist-2026-11-20','pitfall','A page test read the live hunt list and would have broken when the list emptied','S693, 2026-11-20: three page tests read the live hunt block in commons_data.json, so they would have failed the day Sam finished the list, for no fault in the page. They read a fixture now, and a Python check ties the fixture to the builder so the two cannot drift. A test must not read a live worklist.',array['commons','tests','pitfall'],'proposed','PR 3613 (claude/s693-file-handovers, commit 10762b6f)',null,null,'SkyKittiwake (S693)','2026-11-20'),
('p-privacy-hook-names-a-script-2026-11-20','pitfall','The privacy hook refuses a Bash call that names the daily dashboard generator','S693, 2026-11-20: the privacy plugin refuses any Bash call that names the daily dashboard generator, because that script holds the account address as a client identity. Read the script with the Read tool, and keep its name out of shell commands and heredocs (a grep, a python -c, a commit message written by heredoc).',array['privacy','hooks','tooling','pitfall'],'proposed','S693 session transcript (the refusals), 2026-11-20',null,null,'SkyKittiwake (S693)','2026-11-20'),
('p-isolated-agent-starts-in-the-session-directory-2026-11-20','pitfall','A worktree-isolated agent starts in the repo of the session''s working directory','S693, 2026-11-20: a worktree-isolated agent is started in a worktree of whichever repo the session''s working directory is in, and may run git nowhere else. The first checkpoint worker of S693 started in the vault and could do nothing in the tracker. Launch a tracker worker from the tracker.',array['agents','worktree','tooling','pitfall'],'proposed','S693 session transcript, 2026-11-20',null,null,'SkyKittiwake (S693)','2026-11-20')
on conflict (slug) do nothing;

